+// The serial path is a poor carrier for a host that is sequencing in real time.
+// The sub-MCU takes one byte per poll with a fixed inter-byte delay, imitating a
+// 31250-baud line, and its 1024-byte receive buffer has no overflow check:
+// SM_PostSerial advances the write pointer regardless of the read pointer, so
+// anything not yet consumed is silently overwritten. A real cable paces itself;
+// a named pipe does not. Feeding a sequencer through it produced wrong
